---
import Bento from "../../components/grids/Bento.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import Django from "../../components/icons/Django.astro";
import SvelteKit from "../../components/icons/SvelteKit.astro";
import AWS from "../../components/icons/AWS.astro";
import Redis from "../../components/icons/Redis.astro";

const project = {
    name: "Docknote",
    description: "Docker based implementation of the service “Privnote”."
}
---

<ProjectLayout description={project.description} title={project.name}>
    <Section slot="show-section">
        <img class="mx-auto" src="/img/cubes/docknote.webp" />
    </Section>

    <Section slot="tell-section">
        <div class="p-10">
            <p>
                The idea was having a way to setup a way to share private notes that delete on opening them. 
            <p>
            <br>
                By using Docker to setup frontend, backend and the Redis database, everyone can run their own private and secure notes sharing platform using just a single Docker command.
            </p>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section slot="detail-section">
        <div class="flex flex-col h-full p-10">
            <p>
                The application can be set up with a single command <b>“docker compose up -d”</b>.
            <p>
            <br>
                Once running it’s very ease to create new notes, generate a link and have that note destroy itself after being read.
            <p>
            <br>
                For the future I contemplated implementing customization options like auto deletion after a certain amount of time if the note has not been read.
            </p>
            <br>
            <p>
                Notes are only being stored inside a “Redis In-Memory-Database” so they are not actually stored on the drive which makes them basically unrecoverable in case of a system breach for maximum anonymity.
            </p>

            <hr class="my-10">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-2xl">Technologies</h3>
            <br>
            <div class="flex gap-10">
                <SvelteKit />
                <Redis />
            </div>
        </div>
    </Section>
</ProjectLayout>